<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 73,532 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 73,532 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 73,532 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday, compared to 92,094 tonnes on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Saturday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  27,871	    7,695</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  45,661	   84,399</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships are expected to sail and eight to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel    70,000	Chesapeak City     due</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	Capitan Miranda    due</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 25,000	Al-safa		8/7</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,500	Tradewind Express  11/7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
